<title>CANADA: Alberta Agriculture sees 1.215 mln ac unharvested.</title>
<headline>Alberta Agriculture sees 1.215 mln ac unharvested.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alberta Agriculture on Tuesday detailed the number harvested acres compared to planted acres, in thousands of acres.</p>
<p>	 NOVEMBER ALBERTA HARVEST ESTIMATES</p>
<p>	     Planted	  Harvested</p>
<p>W. Wheat	95		 90</p>
<p>S. Wheat   6,850	    6,650</p>
<p>Durum Wheat  800		800</p>
<p>All Wheat  7,745	    7,540</p>
<p>Oats	 1,500	    1,100</p>
<p>Barley     5,900	    5,400</p>
<p>Canola     3,150	    3,000</p>
<p>Fall Rye	80		 70</p>
<p>Spring Rye    20		 10</p>
<p>All Rye	100		 80</p>
<p>Mixed Grains 200		 60</p>
<p>Flaxseed	40		 35</p>
<p>Dry Peas     350		340</p>
<p>Lentils	 25		 25</p>
<p>Hay	  5,350	    5,350</p>
<p>Sugar Beets   35		 35</p>
<p>Color Beans   20		 20</p>
<p>Mustard	105		100</p>
<p>Sunflwr	  3		  3</p>
<p>Canary Sd     25		 25</p>
<p>Fdr Corn	10		 10</p>
<p>TOTAL:    24,260	   23,045</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
